schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "IRS treats cryptocurrency as property, enabling charitable-deduction treatment like cash or stock"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    In the United States, nonprofits can legally accept cryptocurrency
    donations; the IRS treats cryptocurrency as property, so donors can claim
    charitable deductions similar to cash or stock donations. Laws vary by
    country, and the article recommends checking local regulations or a
    nonprofit lawyer.
  evidence: >-
    Attributed in-article to "CryptoAltruists" as the source.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/compliance-legal.md
  interpretation: >-
    Presented as general US-context legal/tax orientation for a nonprofit
    deciding whether to accept crypto, not as jurisdiction-specific legal advice.
  uncertainty: >-
    Single secondary source (CryptoAltruists, a donation-platform-adjacent
    resource hub, not a primary IRS citation); tax law changes over time and
    varies by country — the article itself flags this and recommends
    professional legal counsel.
  maturity: raw
  public_use: not-public-yet
  high_risk: true
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/compliance-legal.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-f8cf63c4e847
